 "url": "https://music.apple.com/au/search?term=Dean+Fraser+Jungle+Flower", "search": true}, {"label": "deezer", "url": "https://www.deezer.com/search/Dean+Fraser+Jungle+Flower", "search": true}, {"label": "discogs", "url": "https://www.discogs.com/search/?q=Dean+Fraser+Jungle+Flower&type=all", "search": true}], "notes": ["“Next up, we're going to have a tune called Jungle Flower by Dean Fraser.”"]}, {"t": null, "time": "--:--:--", "artist": "D'Arcangelo", "title": "Look Out Above", "conf": "low", "links": [{"label": "bandcamp", "url": "https://bandcamp.com/search?q=D%27Arcangelo+Look+Out+Above", "search": true}, {"label": "youtube", "url": "https://www.youtube.com/results?search_query=D%27Arcangelo+Look+Out+Above", "search": true}, {"label": "soundcloud", "url": "https://soundcloud.com/search?q=D%27Arcangelo+Look+Out+Above", "search": true}, {"label": "spotify", "url": "https://open.spotify.com/search/D%27Arcangelo+Look+Out+Above", "search": true}, {"label": "apple", "url": "https://music.apple.com/au/search?term=D%27Arcangelo+Look+Out+Above", "search": true}, {"label": "deezer", "url": "https://www.deezer.com/search/D%27Arcangelo+Look+Out+Above", "search": true}, {"label": "discogs", "url": "https://www.discogs.com/search/?q=D%27Arcangelo+Look+Out+Above&type=all", "search": true}], "notes": ["“dave arju with lookout above at the top”", "mentioned by the presenter but we couldn't work out when it played"]}], "counts": {"high": 9, "mid": 12, "low": 9}, "transcripts": [{"start": "00:00:00", "end": "00:01:58", "text": "Yeah. Yeah, 100%. Can you tell us about any other future plans FAB has for trans inclusion? Well, it's absolutely an ongoing conversation. I think a name change is obviously a very outward facing thing and that does not change internal culture in and of itself. So I think the name change is really about getting people in the door and getting people to be able to come to that first meeting or to be able to engage with us because no amount of internal change is sufficient to get people involved if we can't get them through the door I think that's the big thing but it's absolutely an ongoing conversation internally about what we can do I feel quite supported internally to the collective in the current state of things but that's always got to be an ongoing conversation listening to everyone of every different marginalized identity about how they feel and how the collective is showing up for them. JB, thank you so much for joining us in the studio. It's really exciting to hear trans inclusion getting more airtime, especially over at UCEDD. That was feminist officer Jamie Mazden talking about feminist trans inclusion in universities, particularly over at UCEDD. Back chat. Every Saturday morning on FBI 94.5. But that's all we've got time for today. Of course, a big thanks to our guests, Matthew, Jasmine, Oscar, Sue Higginson, Bevo and Jamie Mazden. And a big thanks to our producers, Holly Payne, Ella Hostie-Snellgrove, Tani Crookshank and Jasper Rady. This has been Back Chat. We'll be back next week with more news from your city and beyond. But until then, stay tuned for some Limbs Akimbo. Up now. Back Chat is produced by FBI Radio in Sydney. Tune in live every Saturday at 9.30am Find more at fbi.radio"}, {"start": "00:11:52", "end": "00:12:11", "text": "Good morning. You're tuned in to FBi Radio 94.5. You're listening to Limbs Akimbo. This is Casey filling in today and taking you through the next two hours. What a pleasure to be here."}, {"start": "00:12:54", "end": "00:13:10", "text": "Masakatsu Takagi, it's called Marginalia No. 65. And then next up we're going to move into a brand new release from Kodak Records Vault, it's called Kongo."}, {"start": "00:30:31", "end": "00:31:58", "text": "Yes, yes, you're here on Limbs Akimbo. My name's Casey. Pleasure to be covering for Jackson today. Thank you for having me, Jackson. Good morning to all my listeners. Sending the biggest love, big kisses and cuddles to Ivy, legend of Sydney radio sin. And jumping off the phone with Nemo in case you missed a shout-out. Don't worry, girl. I got you. And good morning, Nemo. Simon as well. Checking in from Camperdown with Rupert the dog in tow. Happy Saturday and good morning to you. Hope you found a little moment of peace wherever you are this morning. This one is Karen Krogh, Meaning of Love, the Herbert mix. Originally came out in 1971. This is a rework. Yeah, just going to move through some down tempo. Got some goodies for you up till 12 o'clock today. Feel free to text in. Let me know what you're up to. Say what up. It's 0435 123 945."}, {"start": "00:50:19", "end": "00:52:06", "text": "Hi, you're tuned in to FBi Radio 94.5. This is Limbs Akimbo. My name's Casey covering today. Just in the middle of this track called Three Steps by Salah. They're a Ukrainian duo. I believe this came out mid-90s. Before this, we had that Shinichiro Yokota edit, Rayotsu, Jinkou. did you recognize the got to be real sample dave arju with lookout above at the top and then that track from fink called every time i was a kid it seemed i collected something banging track that was the hefner remix yeah casey taking you through till 12 today right here on fbi radio i haven't been inside the building for a couple a couple years now feels good to be back hope you're enjoying the tunes safe travels to everyone out there if you're on the road drive safe next up we're gonna dip into a little bit of like down tempo southern hip-hop uh for the next few tunes a few rarer ones i've found in um the last month the next track is It's called Like a Player, and it's from L.A. Gans. Actually, I'm going to play Days of Burner first by Burner. Keep it locked with me, Casey, right here on FBI Radio 94.5."}, {"start": "01:06:29", "end": "01:07:28", "text": "It ain't cold outside and it's Saturday night tonight. What are you guys getting up to in this gorgeous city of Sydney this week and or tonight? Get at me at the text line. Let me know what's up today. Let me know what you're up to tonight. Halloween, right? Might be a few people out in these streets. 0435 123 945 is the number. This is Casey covering for Jackson this morning. on limbs akimbo coming out of one by sleepy's theme choked out saturday night next up we're gonna have a contemporary hip-hop track from michigan artist georgiana called elevator spaghetti and then we'll dip back into some kind of down-tempo electronic"}, {"start": "01:07:39", "end": "01:07:57", "text": "B-L-A-C-K"}, {"start": "01:18:54", "end": "01:19:56", "text": "Yes, yes, a few shout-outs to give. Loving this track as I mosey around doing laundry and cleaning. Glad to hear you're getting it done. Out to David in the Sydney Coast as well, oiling his deck on this beautiful day. Says he's enjoying the tunes. Thank you, that one we just came out of was Idealist with Bad Times. Before that we had Insha' La by Computer Jockeys. this is a brand new one from tarbo tonic coming out of south africa it's called sunkist hope you get a couple rays on your face today i'm with you till 12 this is casey hey out to joss in bandina thank you for the tunes thank you for listening all right keep it locked you're on fbi 94.5"}, {"start": "01:32:58", "end": "01:33:18", "text": "You're tuned in to Limbs Akimbo right here on FBi Radio 94.5. Broadcasting live from Redfern. This is Casey covering out to Harry in Petersham. Doors and windows open, cleaning the house, radio blaring and loving what you're putting down."}, {"start": "01:33:25", "end": "01:34:22", "text": "I just wanted to jump on the mic before this next track because Cousin is playing next weekend at Soma Festival. Who's going to be there? Sunday, second last set. We're going to be up the front for our boy. And I just remember the first Soma Festival where he played this Hannah track I needed. Absolute classic. And I've been running this one underneath me, also a hannah track h-a-n-n-a it's called the rose it's been bringing me a lot of joy these past few weeks and yeah i just wanted just connecting those two dots excited for cousins set at soma and um yeah just wanted to lay this one down this morning so hope you're enjoying here with you till 12 uh let's get it"}, {"start": "01:37:58", "end": "01:38:13", "text": "Next up we're going to have a brand new one by Don Surf. This is more on like the broken beat tip. It's called Yamaya. And then we'll dip into a few nice old soul ones to close us out."}, {"start": "01:44:43", "end": "01:45:55", "text": "Yep. In the middle of A More Real by John Anderson. Thank you for locking in with me today. It has been an absolute pleasure. Got a special international shout out to send to my girl, Eddie D. She said she's chronically hungover in Tokyo. It be like that. Well, I hope you're having a great trip, B, and hope everyone else out there, wherever you are, having a lovely safe day 15 minutes with me we're gonna smooth it out for the next couple next up I want to play a track from the one and only Barbara Lewis from 1961 this one is On Bended Knees 0435 123 945 if you want to get in touch before I jet this has been Casey covering for cousin today on limbs akimbo keep it locked for saturday lunch after this"}, {"start": "01:52:34", "end": "01:52:53", "text": "Coming out of that one from DJ Rogers, gospel tune from 1977, Love Is All I Need. One more tune for you today before I pass it on over. Next up, we're going to have a tune called Jungle Flower by Dean Fraser."}], "fbi_json": [{"timestamp": {"enabled": true, "formatted": "00:01:58"}, "track": {"title": null, "artists": [{"name": "Limbs Akimbo"}]}, "isPremiere": false, "_confidence": "low"}, {"timestamp": {"enabled": true, "formatted": "00:07:02"}, "track": {"title": "Marginalia #65", "artists": [{"name": "Masakatsu Takagi"}]}, "isPremiere": false, "_confidence": "high"}, {"timestamp": {"enabled": true, "formatted": "00:15:07"}, "track": {"title": "Kongo", "artists": [{"name": "Kodak Records Vault"}]}, 